  "limitations": [
    "This immutable v3 profile preserves the closest HLS datapath and normalizes only the comparison clock/platform contract.",
    "It is execution-driven structural simulation until an exact whole-system HLS variant satisfies the matching-HLS gate.",
    "The profile supports one 19-bit destination partition; larger graphs require the separately modeled partitioned extension.",
    "The 200 MHz kernel and 450 MHz HBM entries describe the requested build configuration; sw_emu does not prove achieved clock or timing closure.",
    "sw_emu event and wall times are not hardware performance evidence.",
    "sw_emu is validated on one eight-vertex workload; the simulator additionally passes ten synthetic microbenchmarks and nine dynamic cases from three compact real-edge slices, but no full real dataset is validated for this profile yet.",
    "The execution-driven simulator implements the full-word update, physical-update reorder, and fixed-round semantics, but its timing is not calibrated cycle-for-cycle against hw.",
    "Graphs beyond one 19-bit destination partition require an explicit partitioned PMA design.",
    "Full PageRank and thresholded residual PageRank are not implemented by this HLS profile.",
    "The eight inherited GraSU ap_uint bitsize warnings remain a synthesis-audit item."
  ],
